### 2. Task outcome (extremely detailed version):
- Chunk processed: indices [47–69] only, per provided bounded payload.
- Inclusion criteria applied: women with a pelvic/adnexal mass suspicious for ovarian cancer; index tests were 
menopausal status, transvaginal ultrasound (USS), serum biomarkers (e.g., CA-125, HE4), and validated multivariable 
models combining these (e.g., RMI, ROMA, IOTA LR2/Simple Rules); appropriate reference standard (histology or clinical 
follow-up); eligible designs were cross-sectional DTA studies, randomized comparisons of tests, or validation studies of
multivariable models.
- Exclusion criteria applied: general screening in asymptomatic populations; prognostic/etiology/genetic predisposition 
papers; treatment or prevention reviews; methodological/meta-analysis papers; guidelines; studies lacking relevant index
tests or appropriate reference standard; studies not focused on women with a suspicious pelvic mass.

Study-level decisions and rationales:
- 47 EXCLUDE: Incidence trends from cancer registry; no DTA design, no index tests, no reference standard in adnexal 
mass cohort.
- 48 EXCLUDE: Systematic review/meta-analysis of preoperative strategies; not a primary DTA/validation study.
- 49 INCLUDE: Prospective DTA of ROMA (HE4+CA-125, menopausal status) in women with adnexal masses; histology reference.
- 50 INCLUDE: Multicentre prospective validation of IOTA LR2/Simple Rules and RMI vs histology; target population and 
tests.
